      "id": "lk3se1j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are electropositive elements that easily lose electrons to form positive ions, while non-metals are electronegative elements.",
        "Metals form basic or amphoteric oxides, whereas non-metals produce acidic or neutral oxides when reacted with oxygen.",
        "The Reactivity Series ranks metals in decreasing order of reactivity, determining displacement reactions and extraction methods.",
        "Highly reactive metals are extracted via electrolysis, moderately reactive metals via reduction with carbon, and low reactivity metals by heating alone.",
        "Ionic compounds formed between metals and non-metals have high melting points and conduct electricity in molten or aqueous states."
      ],
      "id": "soknri8"
    },
